<title>BELGIUM: DEFINANCE SAYS CHAIRMAN TO STEP DOWN.</title>
<headline>DEFINANCE SAYS CHAIRMAN TO STEP DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Definance said on Monday chairman Jean-Jacques De Cloedt intended to leave the board with effect from September 22.</p>
<p>&quot;A board meeting will be convened in September to find a replacement for Mr De Cloedt and to elect a new chairman,&quot; Definance said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
